<!--
  NeurOne PostHog — ClickHouse user for the erasure relay
  NP-ANALYTICS-001 §7.6 (OI-ANALYTICS-01)
  Path: /etc/clickhouse-server/users.d/np-erase-user.xml

  The relay (erase_relay.py) deletes withdrawn people's events and nothing else. Its user may ALTER ... DELETE on the events
  table, and read that table's distinct_id column so the relay can tell an ID whose events are gone (answer 200) from one still
  held (queue it, answer 202) without keeping a list of erased IDs (OI-PRIV-48). It cannot read any other column, insert or
  drop. The column read lets whoever holds this password list the pseudonymous IDs the store holds; that is the price of keeping
  no list of erased IDs (OI-PRIV-48). The password comes from the container's environment (ERASE_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD, set in
  .env). The table name must match ERASE_TABLES and the schema of the PostHog commit pinned in posthog-pin.json.

  WHO MAY CONNECT (OI-PRIV-50): the relay's container only, by its compose service name, never an address range. ClickHouse
  resolves a <host> name when a client connects and admits the client only if its address is one the name resolves to; in a
  compose network the name `erase-relay` is answered by Docker's DNS with the relay's own address and nothing else, so another
  container on analytics-internal that has this password is refused. A name that does not resolve admits nobody (fail closed).
  A name, not a fixed address, so the rule needs no subnet and carries into any compose file whose relay service keeps this
  name and shares a network with ClickHouse (OI-ANALYTICS-03): renaming the service means changing this line in the same
  change. ci/test_posthog_infra.py P11 holds the two together. `docker compose run` does not give its container the service
  name unless it is given the use-aliases option, so the relay self-check is run with that option (np_analytics_001 §7.6).
-->
<clickhouse>
  <users>
    <np_erase>
      <password from_env="ERASE_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD"/>
      <networks><host>erase-relay</host></networks>
      <profile>default</profile>
      <quota>default</quota>
      <grants>
        <query>GRANT ALTER DELETE ON posthog.sharded_events</query>
        <query>GRANT SELECT(distinct_id) ON posthog.sharded_events</query>
      </grants>
    </np_erase>
  </users>
</clickhouse>
